From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: A file id without st_dev on ps5.

st_dev is not stable on this console. docs/FINDINGS.md measured it on
wineserver's own prefix directory -- server-290bff49-7e78bd one run,
server-290bff65-7e78bd the next, st_ino identical both times -- and said
what to do about it: drop st_dev from the comparison, since a prefix
cannot span devices here anyway.

FSCTL_GET_OBJECT_ID is where it does damage. The loader asks for a file's
object id and hands it to find_fileid_module() to decide whether the file
is already loaded; built from a drifting st_dev, the answer is always no.

GTA IV stops at the same point every run -- t=1.34, after wow64win's
PROCESS_ATTACH and before its own image is loaded -- with the server
serving 2728 REQ_select against six in every run that worked, and the
file trace ending on FSCTL_GET_OBJECT_ID over C:\windows and
C:\windows\system32.

st_ino alone identifies a file here.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 46bf0d69bc..076ec48e91 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -6938,8 +6938,28 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtFsControlFile( HANDLE handle, HANDLE event, PIO_APC_ROUTINE ap
             fstat( fd, &st );
             if (needs_close) close( fd );
             memset( info, 0, sizeof(*info) );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+            /* ⚠ st_ino only. st_dev is not stable on this console: the same
+             * directory answers with a different one from call to call.
+             * docs/FINDINGS.md measured it on wineserver's own prefix
+             * directory -- server-290bff49-7e78bd one run,
+             * server-290bff65-7e78bd the next, st_ino identical both times --
+             * and said what to do: drop it from the comparison, a prefix
+             * cannot span devices here anyway.
+             *
+             * This is the comparison it breaks. The loader asks for a file's
+             * object id and hands it to find_fileid_module() to decide whether
+             * that file is already loaded; built from a drifting st_dev the
+             * answer is always no. GTA IV stops at the same point every run --
+             * t=1.34, after wow64win's PROCESS_ATTACH and before its own image
+             * loads -- with the server serving 2728 REQ_select where every
+             * working run served six, and the file trace ending on
+             * FSCTL_GET_OBJECT_ID over C:\windows and C:\windows\system32. */
+            memcpy( info->ObjectId + 8, &st.st_ino, sizeof(st.st_ino) );
+#else
             memcpy( info->ObjectId, &st.st_dev, sizeof(st.st_dev) );
             memcpy( info->ObjectId + 8, &st.st_ino, sizeof(st.st_ino) );
+#endif
             size = sizeof(*info);
         }
         else status = STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;
